# The admin's route form, in Island Hop.
# The photos come from e2e/files/.
# Don't check whether "Create Route" is enabled here: the form picks the first two ports only
# when they have loaded before it opens, so the answer depends on timing.

Test: Admin opens the form for a new route

  As admin:
    go to routes page
    should see "Routes Management"
    click "Add Route"
    "Add New Ferry Route" dialog should be open
    in "Add New Ferry Route" dialog, should see "Estimated Travel Time"
    in "Add New Ferry Route" dialog, should see "Route Cover Photo"
    press Escape
    "Add New Ferry Route" dialog should be closed


Test: The route form stops before sending when the cover photo is missing

  As admin:
    go to routes page
    click "Add Route"
    in "Add New Ferry Route" dialog, should not see "Loading ports..."
    press Escape
    # Opened again now that the ports have loaded, the form starts with two different ports.
    # (An empty description is stopped by the browser itself, with no message on the page.)
    click "Add Route"
    type "A quick test crossing" in "Route Description"
    click "Create Route"
    should see "Route cover photo is required. Please upload an image."
    backend should not receive any request
    "Add New Ferry Route" dialog should be open


Test: The route form refuses a file that isn't a photo

  As admin:
    go to routes page
    click "Add Route"
    upload "notes.txt" to "Route Cover Photo"
    should see "Invalid file format. Please upload a PNG, JPG, or WEBP image."
    backend should not receive any request
    in "Add New Ferry Route" dialog, should see "Click to upload route photo"


Test: Admin saves a new route and deletes it again

  As admin:
    go to routes page
    click "Add Route"
    in "Add New Ferry Route" dialog, should not see "Loading ports..."
    press Escape
    click "Add Route"
    in "Add New Ferry Route" dialog, choose "Blowing Point, Anguilla" for "From"
    in "Add New Ferry Route" dialog, choose "Fort Bay Harbor, Saba" for "To"
    type "HumanTest route {unique}" in "Route Description"
    upload "cover.png" to "Route Cover Photo"
    in "Add New Ferry Route" dialog, "Replace" button should be visible
    click "Create Route"
    should see "Route created successfully"
    backend should receive POST /api/v1/routes
    backend should reply 201 Created
    remember data.id as route
    at the end, call DELETE /api/v1/routes/{route}
    "Add New Ferry Route" dialog should be closed
    in "Blowing Point, Anguilla to Fort Bay Harbor, Saba" row, click "Open menu"
    click "Delete route"
    in "Delete Ferry Route" dialog, click "Delete Route"
    backend should receive DELETE /api/v1/routes/{route}
    backend should reply 200 OK
    should see "Route deleted successfully"


# Made from the draft that "npm run ht -- discover --gaps --drafts" wrote for the server's 409.
# Blowing Point to Marigot already exists, so nothing is saved.
Test: A route that already exists is refused

  As admin:
    go to routes page
    click "Add Route"
    in "Add New Ferry Route" dialog, should not see "Loading ports..."
    press Escape
    click "Add Route"
    in "Add New Ferry Route" dialog, choose "Blowing Point, Anguilla" for "From"
    in "Add New Ferry Route" dialog, choose "Marigot, Saint Martin" for "To"
    type "HumanTest route {unique}" in "Route Description"
    upload "cover.png" to "Route Cover Photo"
    in "Add New Ferry Route" dialog, "Replace" button should be visible
    click "Create Route"
    backend should receive POST /api/v1/routes
    backend should reply 409 Conflict
    should see "A route from Blowing Point, Anguilla to Marigot, Saint Martin already exists"
    "Add New Ferry Route" dialog should be open

# Made from a draft (Coverage page). Only spaces get past the browser's own "required", so the
# page's own check is what stops it.
Test: The route form stops before sending when the description is only spaces

  As admin:
    go to routes page
    click "Add Route"
    in "Add New Ferry Route" dialog, should not see "Loading ports..."
    press Escape
    click "Add Route"
    in "Add New Ferry Route" dialog, choose "Blowing Point, Anguilla" for "From"
    in "Add New Ferry Route" dialog, choose "Marigot, Saint Martin" for "To"
    type "   " in "Route Description"
    upload "cover.png" to "Route Cover Photo"
    in "Add New Ferry Route" dialog, "Replace" button should be visible
    click "Create Route"
    should see "Route description is required."
    backend should not receive any request


# The test route goes from Blowing Point to Fort Bay Harbor (Saba), a pair no real route uses,
# so pausing it changes nothing a traveller can book. It is deleted again when the test ends.
Test: Admin pauses a route and opens it again

  Given a test route from "Blowing Point, Anguilla" to "Fort Bay Harbor, Saba"

  As admin:
    go to routes page
    in "Blowing Point, Anguilla to Fort Bay Harbor, Saba" row, click "Open menu"
    click "Pause route"
    backend should receive PATCH /api/v1/routes/:id
    backend should reply 200 OK
    should see "Route updated successfully"
    click "Paused"
    in "Blowing Point, Anguilla to Fort Bay Harbor, Saba" row, click "Open menu"
    click "Activate route"
    backend should receive PATCH /api/v1/routes/:id
    backend should reply 200 OK
    # Open again, it leaves the "Paused" list.
    should not see "Blowing Point, Anguilla to Fort Bay Harbor, Saba"
    click "All"
    in "Blowing Point, Anguilla to Fort Bay Harbor, Saba" row, should see "Fort Bay Harbor, Saba"
